# Copy to .env and fill in for local development. Never commit the real .env.
#
# Sourceable as-is (`set -a; source .env; set +a`) — ARGUS_DATABASE_URL below
# expands ARGUS_APP_PASSWORD via normal shell variable substitution, so changing
# the password only needs editing in one place. Order matters: this only works
# because ARGUS_APP_PASSWORD is defined above where it's used below.

# Migration/admin connection — the migration-owning role, not argus_app.
ARGUS_MIGRATE_DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/argus?sslmode=disable

# Password to set on the argus_app Postgres role — applied automatically by
# `hub migrate` when this is set (internal/data/approle.go), no separate script.
ARGUS_APP_PASSWORD=changeme

# App connection. Must match ARGUS_APP_PASSWORD above.
ARGUS_DATABASE_URL=postgres://argus_app:${ARGUS_APP_PASSWORD}@localhost:5432/argus?sslmode=disable

# Optional: skip the printed-once generated password and use a known one for local dev.
# ARGUS_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD=

ARGUS_API_ADDR=:8080

# Optional: AI analysis (internal/llm — see README.md's "AI analysis" section
# and STATUS.md §11). Unset ARGUS_LLM_BASE_URL means the "Analyze" button
# returns a clear 503 instead of pretending to work — not a broken default.
#
# These are now SEED DEFAULTS, not the only source: internal/settings.Resolve
# prefers the org_settings DB row's column (if set) over these env vars, and
# a super-admin can set/change them at runtime via PUT /api/v1/admin/settings
# with no hub restart needed. Leave these unset entirely if you'd rather
# configure everything through that API instead.
# ARGUS_LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# ARGUS_LLM_MODEL=
# ARGUS_LLM_API_KEY=

# Optional: bounds on the investigation loop itself (internal/llm/toolloop.go's
# Investigate) — max model round-trips and wall-clock time limit before an
# analysis stops and reports a partial result. Same SEED DEFAULT / DB-row-
# overrides-env-var precedence as the two above — also settable at runtime via
# PUT /api/v1/admin/settings' "analysis" section, no hub restart needed.
# Defaults to 8 iterations / 180 seconds when neither the DB row nor these are set.
# ARGUS_ANALYSIS_MAX_ITERATIONS=8
# ARGUS_ANALYSIS_TIME_LIMIT_SECONDS=180

# Optional: notify new incidents to a webhook (internal/notify — see README.md's
# "Notifications" section and STATUS.md §12). Unset means each sweep tick is
# simply a no-op — no crash, just no notifications.
#
# Also now a SEED DEFAULT, not the only source — same DB-row-overrides-env-var
# precedence and the same PUT /api/v1/admin/settings runtime-editing path as
# ARGUS_LLM_BASE_URL above. Treat this URL as a secret: a Slack incoming-
# webhook URL embeds a bearer-equivalent token in its path, so
# GET /api/v1/admin/settings only ever reports whether it's configured, never
# the URL itself. A Slack incoming-webhook URL or any generic webhook
# receiver both work; the body is {"text": "..."}.
# ARGUS_NOTIFY_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.slack.com/services/...
